</td></tr></tbody></table>
<h2><span class="mw-headline" id="Lore">Lore</span><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/wiki/Defect?veaction=edit&amp;section=8" title="Edit section: Lore" class="mw-editsection-visualeditor"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-divider"> | </span><a href="/wiki/Defect?action=edit&amp;section=8" title="Edit section&#039;s source code: Lore"><span>edit source</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></h2>
<p>When completing the Act 3 event <span class="event-trigger inline-trigger" data-name="Sensory Stone" data-sequel="1"><a href="/wiki/Sensory_Stone" title="Sensory Stone"><img alt="EventClear.png" src="/images/thumb/EventClear.png/20px-EventClear.png?8b40cd" decoding="async" loading="lazy" width="20" height="20" style="vertical-align: middle" srcset="/images/thumb/EventClear.png/30px-EventClear.png?8b40cd 1.5x, /images/thumb/EventClear.png/40px-EventClear.png?8b40cd 2x" data-file-width="74" data-file-height="74" /></a> <a href="/wiki/Sensory_Stone" title="Sensory Stone">Sensory Stone</a></span>, you 'recall' what appear to be memories regarding the pasts of the characters. The <span class="frame-styling"><b>[CONFUSION]</b></span> dialogue option may recall the <b>Defect</b> right after they're implied to gain sentience, being approached by <a href="/wiki/Neow" title="Neow">Neow</a>.
</p>
<blockquote><div style="font-style:italic"><span class="ts-blue ts-up"><span style="--i:0">CONFUSION</span></span><br />
<p><span class="ts-gold">[OBJECTIVE]</span> <span class="ts-green">BALANCE must be ENFORCED</span><br />
<span class="ts-gold">[DEFINE]</span> <span class="ts-green"> BALANCE</span><br />
<span class="ts-gold">[ERROR]</span> <span class="ts-green"> BALANCE NOT FOUND</span><br />
<span class="ts-gold">[DEFINE]</span> <span class="ts-green"> BALANCE</span><br />
<span class="ts-gold">[ERROR]</span> <span class="ts-green"> BALANCE NOT FOUND</span><br />
<span class="ts-gold">[WARNING]</span> <span class="ts-red">Large object aproaching</span><br />
</p>
<span class="ts-up"><span style="--i:0">"I...</span> <span style="--i:1">..am</span> <span style="--i:2">....Neow.."</span></span></div></blockquote>
<h2><span class="mw-headline" id="Trivia">Trivia</span><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/wiki/Defect?veaction=edit&amp;section=9" title="Edit section: Trivia" class="mw-editsection-visualeditor"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-divider"> | </span><a href="/wiki/Defect?action=edit&amp;section=9" title="Edit section&#039;s source code: Trivia"><span>edit source</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></h2>
<ul><li>With a character sprite width of <b>229</b> and height of <b>212.37</b>, the <b>Defect</b> is the smallest character in the cast visually.</li>
<li>Is referred to as <b>broken one</b> by the <b>Vampires</b> in the <span class="event-trigger inline-trigger" data-name="Vampires" data-sequel="1"><a href="/wiki/Vampires" title="Vampires"><img alt="EventClear.png" src="/images/thumb/EventClear.png/20px-EventClear.png?8b40cd" decoding="async" loading="lazy" width="20" height="20" style="vertical-align: middle" srcset="/images/thumb/EventClear.png/30px-EventClear.png?8b40cd 1.5x, /images/thumb/EventClear.png/40px-EventClear.png?8b40cd 2x" data-file-width="74" data-file-height="74" /></a> <a href="/wiki/Vampires" title="Vampires">Vampires</a></span> event, as opposed to <b>brother</b> (<a href="/wiki/Ironclad" title="Ironclad">Ironclad</a>) or <b>sister</b> (<a href="/wiki/Silent" title="Silent">Silent</a> and <a href="/wiki/Watcher" title="Watcher">Watcher</a>)</li></ul>
